{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 disproof of the Equal Halves conjecture of L. Gillibert (2026): every finite connected vertex-transitive graph of even order would have a partition V = A ⊔ B into nonempty sets with G[A] and G[B] connected and isomorphic (induced subgraphs). The counterexample is graph 2659 of the Holt–Royle census of vertex-transitive graphs on 28 vertices (9-regular, automorphism group of order 504, not a Cayley graph). The kernel checks that for no vertex set A are G[A] and G[Aᶜ] isomorphic: an isomorphism would give an involution preserving same-side degree, triangle and distance-two counts, and 15 tests on these statistics, evaluated on all 2-colourings up to the stabiliser of a vertex, rule this out.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Ming-Chih Kao"
    }
  ],
